{
    "_doc": "Occupations of the townsfolk (systems/townJobs.js, world/innerMap/townWork.js). Every grown resident of a town with a roster holds one (p.job = { id, rank, since, master?, employer?, hired? }), assigned to fit the town: plan[type] is the order the town fills its trades in (occupation ids, repeated for a second hand), as far as it has grown people of a fitting role; an occupation's land ('water', 'hills', 'pasture', 'forest') must be near or its places go to the next. roles: who may hold it (their roster role); role: the role an apprentice takes on coming of age. work: what they do at it on the map — field, herd, fish, chop, mine, prop (stand at a prop by their workplace: props, with activity), inside (in the workplace: furniture they use), stall, carry, sweep, wash, beg, none. workplaces: building types (their own first). hours: the day profile (hours[...]). goods / recipes: the market goods it brings in and the trades (data/markets.json recipes) it works — the town's output of them scales with the hands at it (crew: staff weight against the plan's count, floor + (1 - floor) * min(cap, ratio) ^ elasticity). wage: coin a day at master rank; pay: who pays (sales: the town's buyers out of the town purse; master: their master; employer: the household or house they serve; town: the town purse; none). say: their answer to 'What's your work?' ({place}, {master}, {years}, {town}). barks: said at work now and then (barkChance, barkGap seconds per person).",
    "enabled": true,
